From 2f487f61a8f4a3aad667db22f7da2df141e3ae0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hermes Agent <hermes-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 13:18:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(gateway): bind session context for plugin slash
 commands
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A plugin-registered slash command cannot see the origin it was invoked
from. `_handle_message` calls `reset_session_vars()` at handler entry so a
task that inherited a concurrent sibling's ContextVars starts clean, and
binds this turn's identity via `_set_session_env` only much later, on the
agent path. The plugin branch sits between the two and dispatches
`plugin_handler(user_args)` — a positional string, no `event`, no
`source`. A handler calling `get_session_env("HERMES_SESSION_PLATFORM")`
therefore finds the ContextVar unset and falls through to process-global
`os.environ` (resolution step 2 in `gateway/session_context`).

`os.environ` is last-writer-wins for the whole process, so on a gateway
serving several platforms concurrently a plugin command reads whichever
session's identity was mirrored most recently. Reproducible symptom: two
concurrent sessions on different platforms, each running a plugin command
that reads `HERMES_SESSION_PLATFORM` — both observe the same foreign
value, never their own.

Extract the field mapping out of `_set_session_env` into
`_set_session_env_from_source(source, session_key)` and have
`_set_session_env` delegate to it (no behaviour change; it was already
reading nothing but `context.source` and `context.session_key`), then
bind that around plugin dispatch using the `_quick_key` already in scope,
clearing it in a `finally`. Async handlers keep working, a falsy result
still suppresses the echo, and a raising handler still falls through to
skill resolution as before — only now without leaving the binding behind.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
